[h1]D'thorga Medical[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.37.1
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published yet - draft held for the owner's review

[h2]Read this first (gotchas)[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Partly tested in game:[/b] burns, dosing, the oxygen concentrator, the burn unit bed and the save bridge on the five earlier mods this one replaces; and on this mod, radiation control, doctors' work with many wounded, field care giving way to the carry, and radiation sickness running its real course and converting once. Everything else is [b]not yet tested in game[/b].
[*][b]Needs Harmony, D'thorga Framework (0.184.0 or later) and Vanilla Expanded Framework, loaded before it.[/b] The mod asks for that order itself, so RimSort and the game's sorter get it right. [b]RimWorld 1.7 only.[/b]
[*][b]Vanilla Gravship Expanded is strongly recommended[/b] (it needs the Odyssey expansion). Six oxygen pieces use its canisters and pipes and exist only with it; without it a letter says so once.
[*][b]Optional, used when present:[/b] More Injuries, Combat Extended, Search and Rescue, VFE Medical, Dubs Bad Hygiene, Dubs Rimatomics, Useful Marks and Hospitality. None is needed.
[*][b]Combat Extended:[/b] its own smoke condition applies by default; a setting adds this mod's smoke inhalation as well.
[*][b]It replaces five earlier mods[/b] (D'thorga Burns and Smoke, Emergency Dosing, Triage, Medical Equipment and Medical Save Bridge). [b]Switch all five off and this one on in the same change.[/b] Your colony and your settings carry over.
[*][b]Safe to add to a running colony.[/b]
[*][b]Taking it out of a colony:[/b] press Remove every condition this mod adds, from every pawn in its settings, deconstruct its machines and burn unit beds, take its items out of the colony, save, then switch the mod off.
[*][b]Adding More Injuries to a running colony asks first:[/b] Convert now, Not now or Never for this save. [b]Back up the save first.[/b] [b]If you choose Not now, do not save that colony[/b]: whatever went wrong on that load is kept when you save.
[*][b]With Dubs Rimatomics,[/b] this mod's radiation model takes over radiation for people and converts anyone's existing radiation once. Switching it off, or removing the mod, does not bring Rimatomics' conditions back.
[*][b]Decide before a colony:[/b] People in pain fetch their own painkillers (on: check your drug policies first, as addiction and overdose are real); tox gas is slow-acting by default; doctors may operate without orders to save life for colonists, slaves and prisoners, never for guests; How much to show is Plain, with no percentages or hours.
[*][b]What bites in play:[/b] carbon monoxide ignores gas masks, and a patient on oxygen still breathes the room's air. Fires in the open cause heatstroke and burns nearby. Oxygen canisters explode when they burn. No surgery in the hyperbaric chamber. With Search and Rescue, give your medics kits to carry.
[/list]

[h2]What it does[/h2]
Burns and smoke that matter, doctors who dose and operate on their own, hospital and field equipment to treat it all, and a safe way to add More Injuries to a colony you are already playing. Built to sit beside More Injuries and Combat Extended; neither is required.
[list]
[*][b]Burns and smoke:[/b] every burn adds up to a burned body fraction. Past about a sixth of the body, burn shock kills within days unless the burns are tended, the patient rests and gets fluids. Airway burns swell over hours and can close the throat; smoke damages the lungs for days; carbon monoxide from fires lingers in closed rooms; fires heat the air around them.
[*][b]Tox gas and acid:[/b] tox gas injures eyes, throat, lungs and skin; acid keeps burning until a safety shower washes it off.
[*][b]Emergency dosing:[/b] doctors give the best pain relief within reach, a sedative in extreme pain, and a drug that speeds immunity to a patient losing the race against a deadly disease. Nothing is given while an earlier dose still works or where it would be dangerous. Any mod's drugs qualify, found by what they do.
[*][b]Triage:[/b] doctors queue the life-saving operation a patient needs, never riskier than you allow, and take the worst case first. When no one can operate, a message says what is missing. Each person has a button for how far doctors may go without orders.
[*][b]Equipment:[/b] oxygen concentrator, ventilator, burn unit bed, silver burn dressing, manual resuscitator, safety shower, gas alarm and field kits; with Vanilla Gravship Expanded, a bedside oxygen stand, a hyperbaric chamber, a field oxygen kit, an oxygen electrolyser and a liquid oxygen store.
[*][b]Radiation:[/b] radiation sickness in its real course, where care decides who lives, late effects (each a setting) and three medicines doctors give by themselves. With Dubs Rimatomics, a line where colonists suit up before going in.
[*][b]Colonies saved before More Injuries:[/b] converts every wound, lost limb and bionic onto the right part, so More Injuries' first-load clean-up cannot wipe wounds or raise the dead.
[/list]

Every part has its own page in the settings window, with a search box. How to play it is in the [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-rimworld/blob/main/docs/player-guide/medical.md]player guide's Medical chapter[/url].

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]RimWorld 1.7
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2009463077]Harmony[/url]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2023507013]Vanilla Expanded Framework[/url]
[*]D'thorga Framework, 0.184.0 or later
[/list]
Strongly recommended: Vanilla Gravship Expanded (needs Odyssey).

